{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>From the El of your father.</b> In my opinion it is joined with the verse above, and the meaning is: this power that was in your hand — it was from the El of your father, and He will help you. And the mem of מאל is servile to itself and to what follows it, like \"באל שדי ושמי ד׳\" (Exodus 6:3). So the meaning is doubled: ומאת שדי, and He will bless you. The Gaon [Saadia] interpreted: I will ask of the El of your father. And it is possible that ברכת שמים is joined with מאל אביך, and the meaning will be clarified by the word תהיין." "ברכת תהום — as Moses said, וממגד ארץ (Deuteronomy 33:16). Also תהום is feminine, as in \"תהום רוממתחו\" (Ezekiel 31:4). And so its meaning is that rains descend from above upon his land, and the springs and streams multiply from the tehom, which lies beneath the earth:" "<b>Blessings of breasts and womb.</b> He likened the breasts to heaven and the womb to the tehom, and the meaning is that his sons multiply. And the opposite of this: \"רחם משכיל ושדים צומקים\" (Hosea 9:14)."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {0 "Resolved הגאון as Saadia by standard convention."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:48:38.449929113Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}